{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Sing</b> — Since David is a ḥasid, as it is written: \"and you will not give your ḥasid over\" — the kindnesses of David will bring good tidings to the ḥasidim, that if what happened to him happens to them, HaShem will deliver them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Psalm 16:10 (לא תתן חסידך); the phrase 'חסדי דוד יבשר החסידים' is compressed, possibly a wordplay linking David's name/merits to the good tidings for the ḥasidim. Transmitted hyper-literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:58.353256068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}